    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented both functions in `app/network.py`. The 3 existing tests pass. A smoke check with a stub transport also passed: the job header and huggingface_hub's user agent were both sent, the timeouts came out as 5s connect and 60s everywhere else, a timeout returned `None` with a warning on `app.network`, and a missing repo still raised `RepositoryNotFoundError`. I haven't added any tests for these functions to the suite.\n\n**`configure_hub_http(transport=None)`**\n- It uses huggingface_hub's `set_client_factory` to give it an `httpx2.Client` (2.0.0 uses the `httpx2` package, not `httpx`). huggingface_hub creates that client once and shares it across every `HfApi` instance.\n- The header `X-Acme-Job: nightly-sync` is set on the client, so it's merged with huggingface_hub's own per-request headers.\n- The stub transport, when given, is passed straight to the client.\n- huggingface_hub's own request hook is kept, so offline mode and request IDs still work. That hook is only in a private module (`huggingface_hub.utils._http`), which is fine while the version stays pinned.\n\n**Timeouts need a second step.** Setting the timeout on the client isn't enough. `HfApi.model_info` and other methods pass `timeout=None` explicitly on each request, and `httpx2` reads that as \"no timeout\", which replaces the client's setting. A second request hook therefore sets the 5s/60s timeouts on every request just before it's sent. As a result, a `timeout=` passed to an individual `HfApi` call is also overridden.\n\n**`current_revision(repo_id)`** calls `HfApi().model_info(repo_id, revision=\"main\").sha`. It catches only `httpx2.TimeoutException` and `httpx2.NetworkError`, which includes connection failures. For those it logs a warning and returns `None`. Everything else is raised, including 404s, auth errors and offline mode.\n\nI couldn't delete the scratch script `_chk.py` in the project root because the `rm` command needed approval. Please remove it."
